Maps
----
suwalki.tres – Suwalki Lakeland around Szurpily (Suwalki Landscape Park, Poland), 30x24 hexes
of 250 m, UTM 34N. Real data, downloaded 2026-10-31:
  DEM tile Copernicus_DSM_COG_10_N54_00_E022_00_DEM
  OSM extract (Overpass, bbox 54.20580,22.81264,54.26417,22.94746)
  Rebuild: tools/import_map.py --center=54.235,22.88 --size=30x24 --hex=250 --name=suwalki
           --display-name="Suwalki Lakeland (Szurpily)" --out=data/maps/suwalki.tres
  (a re-download gets today's OpenStreetMap, so the result may differ from the committed file)
  Re-imported 2026-10-31 (TASK-108: fields / urban / marsh, road and river links) offline from
  the same cached inputs with --offline added to the command above.

suwalki_theatre.tres – the operational theatre around the Suwalki Gap (north-east Poland, the
Kaliningrad oblast, southern Lithuania, western Belarus), 68x64 hexes of 5 km, UTM 34N for the
whole map, centre 54.20 N 22.888 E (TASK-092a; 0.012 deg west of the decided 22.90 E so that
Kaliningrad sits 2 hexes inside the west edge). Real data, downloaded 2026-11-02 (66 OSM tiles
and the DEM) and 2026-11-07 (the last 6 OSM tiles, 55.0-55.5 N 23.0-26.0 E):
  DEM: 24 Copernicus GLO-90 tiles Copernicus_DSM_COG_30_N52..N55_00_E020..E025_00_DEM
       (elevation: Copernicus GLO-90 DEM, produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-90 (c) DLR e.V.
       2010-2014 and (c) Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by
       the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved; free use with this attribution under
       the Copernicus DEM GLO-90 licence, tiles from https://copernicus-dem-90m.s3.amazonaws.com)
  OSM: 72 Overpass tiles of 0.5 x 0.5 degrees (52.5-55.5 N, 20.0-26.0 E; the operational
       query: forest, water, wetland, urban land use, major roads, rivers, coastline, country
       borders), 1.85 GB in the cache; plus 72 borders-only tiles (country borders, TASK-113)
  Rebuild: tools/import_map.py --profile=operational --center=54.20,22.888 --size=68x64
           --name=suwalki_theatre --display-name="Suwalki Gap theatre"
           --out=data/maps/suwalki_theatre.tres
           --countries=PL:54.10,22.93,LT:54.90,23.90,BY:53.68,23.83,RU:54.71,20.51
  (the committed file was imported 2026-11-07 with --offline added, with the profile's tuned
  default thresholds; sea filled from the default seeds 55.30 N 20.60 E and 55.10 N 21.05 E;
  countries (TASK-113) from the seed points Suwalki, Kaunas, Grodno, Kaliningrad - the default
  of --countries, spelled out here - and the country borders of OpenStreetMap: 72 more
  Overpass tiles "bd1_*" with only the member ways of the admin_level=2 border relations)
  (re-imported offline from the same cache on 2026-11-07 for the graphic layers, TASK-126: water,
  land cover and relief images; the hex data is unchanged)
  (a re-download gets today's OpenStreetMap, so the result may differ from the committed file)

suwalki_tactical/ (layer.tres + chunk_<cx>_<cy>.tres) - the tactical layer of the whole
suwalki_theatre area (TASK-094b): 1370x1288 hexes of 250 m, UTM 34N, centre 54.20 N 22.888 E (the
theatre's centre), in 128 x 128 chunks; contact battles are cut out of it. Made OFFLINE from the
same cached inputs as suwalki_theatre.tres (the 72 operational OSM tiles "op1_*" - forest, water,
wetland, urban land use, major roads, rivers, coastline - and the 24 Copernicus GLO-90 tiles, see
above; no farmland / grass and no minor roads in these inputs). Imported 2026-11-08:
  Rebuild: tools/import_map.py --profile=layer --center=54.20,22.888 --size=1370x1288
           --name=suwalki_tactical --display-name="Suwalki Gap theatre (tactical layer)"
           --out=data/maps/suwalki_tactical --offline

